---
import Page from '../../layouts/Page.astro';
import ScoreHistory from '../../components/ScoreHistory.astro';
import SharedResults from '../../components/SharedResults.astro';

const items = [
	{ id: 'clouding', text: 'Mental clouding (brain fog, difficulty thinking clearly)' },
	{ id: 'vision', text: 'Blurred vision' },
	{ id: 'dyspnoea', text: 'Shortness of breath' },
	{ id: 'heartbeat', text: 'Rapid heartbeat' },
	{ id: 'tremor', text: 'Tremulousness (shakiness)' },
	{ id: 'chest', text: 'Chest discomfort' },
	{ id: 'headache', text: 'Headache' },
	{ id: 'lightheaded', text: 'Lightheadedness' },
	{ id: 'nausea', text: 'Nausea' },
];
---

<Page
	title="Vanderbilt Orthostatic Symptom Score (VOSS): free online POTS symptom rating"
	description="Rate the nine VOSS symptoms from 0 to 10 while upright and get your Vanderbilt Orthostatic Symptom Score (0–90) instantly, with reference values from POTS trials and healthy controls. The standing symptom score used in Vanderbilt and Calgary POTS studies. Free, no sign-up."
>
	<Fragment slot="head">
			<script type="application/ld+json">
	{
	  "@context": "https://schema.org",
	  "@graph": [
	    {
	      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
	      "itemListElement": [
	        {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://www.postviralrecovery.com/"},
	        {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Tools", "item": "https://www.postviralrecovery.com/tools/"},
	        {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Vanderbilt Orthostatic Symptom Score", "item": "https://www.postviralrecovery.com/tools/vanderbilt-orthostatic-symptom-score/"}
	      ]
	    },
	    {
	      "@type": "FAQPage",
	      "mainEntity": [
	        {
	          "@type": "Question",
	          "name": "What is the Vanderbilt Orthostatic Symptom Score?",
	          "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The VOSS is a nine-symptom rating used in POTS research from the Vanderbilt Autonomic Dysfunction Center. Each symptom (mental clouding, blurred vision, shortness of breath, rapid heartbeat, tremulousness, chest discomfort, headache, lightheadedness, nausea) is rated from 0 (absent) to 10 (worst you have experienced) at a moment in time, usually at the end of a stand or tilt test. The total runs from 0 to 90."}
	        },
	        {
	          "@type": "Question",
	          "name": "What is a high VOSS score?",
	          "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "There is no validated cut-off. In published studies, people with POTS have scored around 26 on average after ten minutes of head-up tilt and a median of about 35 after a stand test, while healthy adults averaged about 12 after ten minutes of tilt. Treatments that helped in trials moved the score by around 5 to 14 points."}
	        },
	        {
	          "@type": "Question",
	          "name": "How is the VOSS different from the Malmö POTS score or COMPASS-31?",
	          "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "The VOSS measures symptoms right now, typically while standing, which makes it a test-day measure that pairs with a NASA lean test or tilt. The Malmö POTS Symptom Score covers the past seven days and the COMPASS-31 covers a longer period across six autonomic domains. They answer different questions: acute orthostatic burden versus weekly or overall symptom load."}
	        }
	      ]
	    }
	  ]
	}
			</script>
	</Fragment>
			<div class="tool-header">
				<a href="/tools" class="section-label tools">Tools</a>
				<h1>Vanderbilt Orthostatic Symptom Score (VOSS)</h1>
				<p class="subtitle">Nine symptoms rated 0–10 while upright: the standing symptom score from POTS trials</p>
				<p class="description">
					The Vanderbilt Orthostatic Symptom Score comes from the Vanderbilt Autonomic Dysfunction Center, where Satish Raj and colleagues used it in POTS drug studies from 2005 onwards. It has since been used in the Calgary compression garment trial, exercise studies in post-COVID POTS, and a growing list of others. You rate nine symptoms from <strong>0 (absent)</strong> to <strong>10 (the worst you have experienced)</strong> for how you feel <strong>right now</strong>. The total runs from 0 to 90.
				</p>
				<p class="description">
					Unlike the weekly <a href="/tools/malmo-pots-score/">Malmö POTS score</a> or the broader <a href="/tools/compass-31/">COMPASS-31</a>, the VOSS is a snapshot. In trials it is completed at the end of a 10-minute stand or tilt, which makes it a natural companion to the <a href="/tools/nasa-lean-test/">NASA lean test</a>: rate your symptoms at the end of the standing phase and you have a symptom number to sit alongside the heart-rate numbers. Rated lying down and again after standing, the difference shows how much standing itself drives your symptoms.
				</p>
				<div class="disclaimer">
					<strong>This is not a diagnostic tool.</strong> The VOSS has no validated cut-off and no formal validation study; it is used in research as a change measure. Healthy people report symptoms after a prolonged tilt too, so a non-zero score is expected. It cannot tell POTS apart from other causes of orthostatic symptoms. Discuss your results with your doctor. Based on: Raj SR, Black BK, Biaggioni I, Harris PA, Robertson D. <em>Acetylcholinesterase inhibition improves tachycardia in postural tachycardia syndrome.</em> Circulation. 2005;111(21):2734–2740; and Raj SR, et al. <em>Propranolol decreases tachycardia and improves symptoms in POTS: less is more.</em> Circulation. 2009;120(9):725–734. Instruction wording on this page is our own; the score is described in those papers rather than distributed as a form.
				</div>
			</div>

			<form id="voss-form" novalidate>
				<div class="context" data-id="context">
					<p class="symptom-text">When are you rating these symptoms?</p>
					<div class="radio-options">
						<label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="context" value="rest" /><span><strong>At rest</strong> — lying or sitting, before standing</span></label>
						<label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="context" value="short" /><span><strong>Standing, less than 10 minutes</strong></span></label>
						<label class="radio-label"><input type="radio" name="context" value="stand" /><span><strong>At the end of a 10-minute stand or tilt</strong> — as in the trials, e.g. the last minute of a NASA lean test</span></label>
					</div>
				</div>

				<p class="form-instructions">Rate how severe each symptom is <strong>right now</strong>, where 0 = absent and 10 = the worst you have experienced.</p>
				{items.map(item => (
					<div class="symptom" data-id={item.id}>
						<p class="symptom-text">{item.text}</p>
						<div class="segmented">
							{Array.from({ length: 11 }, (_, v) => (
								<label>
									<input type="radio" name={item.id} value={v} aria-label={v === 0 ? '0: absent' : v === 10 ? '10: worst you have experienced' : String(v)} />
									<span aria-hidden="true">{v}</span>
								</label>
							))}
						</div>
					</div>
				))}

				<div class="form-footer">
					<button type="submit">Calculate my score</button>
					<button type="button" id="reset-btn">Clear all</button>
				</div>
			</form>

			<div id="results" class="results" hidden>
				<h2>Your VOSS score</h2>
				<div class="total-score">
					<span id="total-score-value">—</span>
					<span class="total-score-label">out of 90</span>
				</div>
				<p id="score-interpretation" class="score-interp"></p>
				<p id="compare" class="compare" hidden></p>

				<h3>Symptom breakdown</h3>
				<div id="chart" class="chart"></div>

				<div class="results-disclaimer">
					<h3>Understanding your score</h3>
					<p>Published reference points, all rated while upright: healthy adults after 10 minutes of head-up tilt averaged about 12 (SD 12); people with POTS after 10 minutes of tilt averaged 26 (SD 17) without compression and 12 with full abdominal and leg compression (Bourne 2021); POTS patients after a stand test scored a median of about 35; and people with post-COVID POTS averaged 41 after an active stand, falling to 33 after a 12-week exercise programme. A mild unselected post-COVID cohort scored a median of 1 while standing.</p>
					<p>Treatment effects in trials were around 5–14 points, so a change of that size between two ratings under the same conditions is the kind of difference the studies treated as meaningful. There is no cut-off that identifies POTS: that needs the heart-rate response recorded by a stand or tilt test.</p>
					<p>To use the VOSS as a tracker, keep the conditions constant: same time of day, same posture, same duration standing. Rating at rest and then at the end of a standing period, and noting both, gives you the orthostatic component specifically. Record scores in a note or the <a href="/tools/trackers/stand-test-logger/">stand test logger</a> alongside your heart-rate readings.</p>
					<p><strong>This is not a diagnosis.</strong> Discuss your results with your doctor or specialist.</p>
				</div>

				<ScoreHistory toolId="vanderbilt-orthostatic-symptom-score" toolName="VOSS" />

				<button type="button" id="back-btn" class="back-btn">Edit answers</button>
			</div>

			<SharedResults toolId="vanderbilt-orthostatic-symptom-score" />
</Page>

<script>
import { vanderbiltOrthostaticSymptomScore, VOSS_CONTEXT_CODES } from '../../tools/vanderbilt-orthostatic-symptom-score';
import { mountScoreHistory, mountSharedResults } from '../../scripts/results/scoreHistory';

const ITEMS = [
	{ id: 'clouding', text: 'Mental clouding' },
	{ id: 'vision', text: 'Blurred vision' },
	{ id: 'dyspnoea', text: 'Shortness of breath' },
	{ id: 'heartbeat', text: 'Rapid heartbeat' },
	{ id: 'tremor', text: 'Tremulousness' },
	{ id: 'chest', text: 'Chest discomfort' },
	{ id: 'headache', text: 'Headache' },
	{ id: 'lightheaded', text: 'Lightheadedness' },
	{ id: 'nausea', text: 'Nausea' },
];
const KEY = 'pvr-voss-last';
let lastRecordedContext: string | null = null;

const form = document.getElementById('voss-form') as HTMLFormElement;
const results = document.getElementById('results') as HTMLElement;

const history = mountScoreHistory(vanderbiltOrthostaticSymptomScore);
mountSharedResults(vanderbiltOrthostaticSymptomScore);

function getVal(id: string): number | null {
	const checked = form.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>(`input[name="${id}"]:checked`);
	return checked ? parseInt(checked.value, 10) : null;
}
function getStr(id: string): string | null {
	const checked = form.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>(`input[name="${id}"]:checked`);
	return checked ? checked.value : null;
}
function flag(id: string, selector: string) {
	const el = form.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`${selector}[data-id="${id}"]`);
	el?.classList.add('missing');
	el?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'center' });
	setTimeout(() => el?.classList.remove('missing'), 2500);
}

form.addEventListener('submit', (e) => {
	e.preventDefault();
	if (!getStr('context')) { flag('context', '.context'); return; }
	for (const item of ITEMS) {
		if (getVal(item.id) === null) { flag(item.id, '.symptom'); return; }
	}
	const context = getStr('context')!;
	const values = ITEMS.map(it => ({ item: it, val: getVal(it.id)! }));
	const total = values.reduce((s, v) => s + v.val, 0);

	(document.getElementById('total-score-value') as HTMLElement).textContent = String(total);

	const ctxLabel = context === 'rest' ? 'at rest' : context === 'short' ? 'standing for under 10 minutes' : 'at the end of a 10-minute stand';
	let interp = `Your VOSS score is ${total} out of 90, rated ${ctxLabel}. `;
	if (context === 'stand') {
		if (total >= 26) interp += 'This is at or above the average of 26 reported for people with POTS after 10 minutes of head-up tilt, and well above the healthy-control average of 12. It indicates a substantial orthostatic symptom burden on this occasion.';
		else if (total > 12) interp += 'This sits between the healthy-control average of 12 and the POTS average of 26 after 10 minutes of tilt. Symptoms are present with standing but the burden on this occasion was moderate.';
		else interp += 'This is at or below the average of 12 reported for healthy adults after 10 minutes of tilt. Standing produced few or mild symptoms on this occasion.';
	} else if (context === 'short') {
		interp += 'Trials rate the VOSS after a full 10 minutes upright, and symptoms typically build over that time, so a short-stand score will usually understate your 10-minute score. Use it for comparison with your own earlier ratings under the same conditions.';
	} else {
		if (total >= 20) interp += 'This is a high resting score. Vanderbilt studies report seated baselines in POTS of roughly 14–27, so symptoms are substantial even before standing. Rating again at the end of a stand will show how much orthostatic stress adds.';
		else if (total >= 5) interp += 'Some symptoms are present at rest. Rating again at the end of a 10-minute stand, and comparing the two numbers, shows the orthostatic component.';
		else interp += 'Few symptoms at rest. The VOSS is most informative when repeated at the end of a 10-minute stand, so that the difference between the two shows what standing itself does.';
	}
	(document.getElementById('score-interpretation') as HTMLElement).textContent = interp;

	// Compare with a saved rating under a different condition from the same day.
	const compare = document.getElementById('compare') as HTMLElement;
	compare.hidden = true;
	try {
		const raw = localStorage.getItem(KEY);
		if (raw) {
			const prev = JSON.parse(raw) as { date: string; context: string; total: number };
			const sameDay = prev.date.slice(0, 10) === new Date().toISOString().slice(0, 10);
			if (sameDay && prev.context !== context) {
				const prevLabel = prev.context === 'rest' ? 'at rest' : prev.context === 'short' ? 'standing under 10 minutes' : 'at the end of a 10-minute stand';
				compare.innerHTML = `Earlier today you scored <strong>${prev.total}</strong> ${prevLabel}. The difference between the two is <strong>${Math.abs(total - prev.total)}</strong> points.`;
				compare.hidden = false;
			}
		}
		localStorage.setItem(KEY, JSON.stringify({ date: new Date().toISOString(), context, total }));
	} catch { /* storage unavailable */ }

	(document.getElementById('chart') as HTMLElement).innerHTML = values.map(v => `
		<div class="chart-row">
			<div class="chart-label">${v.item.text}</div>
			<div class="chart-track"><div class="chart-bar" style="width:${Math.max(2, v.val * 10)}%"></div></div>
			<div class="chart-val">${v.val}</div>
		</div>`).join('');

	form.hidden = true;
	results.hidden = false;
	// A rating in a different context (e.g. after standing, following one at
	// rest) is a separate result, not an edit of the earlier one.
	if (lastRecordedContext !== null && lastRecordedContext !== context) history.startNew();
	lastRecordedContext = context;
	history.record({
		total,
		subscores: { ...Object.fromEntries(values.map(v => [v.item.id, v.val])), context: VOSS_CONTEXT_CODES[context] },
		summary: `VOSS ${total} out of 90, rated ${ctxLabel}`,
	});
	results.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
});

document.getElementById('reset-btn')?.addEventListener('click', () => form.reset());
document.getElementById('back-btn')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
	results.hidden = true;
	form.hidden = false;
	form.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
});
</script>

<style>
	.tool-header { padding-bottom: 1.5em; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); margin-bottom: 2em; }
	.tool-header h1 { margin: 0.3em 0 0.1em; }
	.subtitle { color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-size: 1.05em; margin: 0 0 0.75em; }
	.description { margin-bottom: 1em; }

	.form-instructions { font-size: 0.88em; color: rgb(var(--gray-dark)); background: var(--accent-light); border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.7em 1.1em; margin-bottom: 1.25em; }

	.context, .symptom { border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); border-radius: 8px; padding: 0.9em 1.2em; margin-bottom: 0.65em; transition: border-color 0.15s, box-shadow 0.15s; }
	.context { margin-bottom: 1.25em; }
	.missing { border-color: #c0392b !important; box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(192, 57, 43, 0.12); }
	.symptom-text { margin: 0 0 0.7em; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.95em; line-height: 1.4; }

	.radio-options { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5em; }
	.radio-label { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 0.6em; padding: 0.6em 0.8em; border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); border-radius: 6px; cursor: pointer; font-size: 0.92em; line-height: 1.4; }
	.radio-label:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
	.radio-label:has(input:checked) { background: var(--accent-light); border-color: var(--accent); }
	.radio-label input { margin-top: 0.25em; }

	.segmented { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(11, 1fr); gap: 0.3em; max-width: 32em; }
	.segmented label { position: relative; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-size: 0.88em; padding: 0.45em 0; border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); border-radius: 5px; cursor: pointer; transition: background 0.1s, border-color 0.1s; }
	.segmented label:hover { border-color: var(--accent); }
	.segmented input { position: absolute; opacity: 0; width: 0; height: 0; }
	.segmented label:has(input:checked) { background: var(--accent-light); border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent-dark); font-weight: 700; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--accent); }

	.form-footer { display: flex; gap: 1em; padding: 1.5em 0 1em; }
	button[type="submit"] { background: var(--accent); color: #fff; border: none; padding: 0.75em 2em; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 1em; font-weight: 700; cursor: pointer; font-family: inherit; }
	button[type="submit"]:hover { background: var(--accent-dark); }
	button[type="button"] { background: none; border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); padding: 0.75em 1.5em; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 0.95em; cursor: pointer; color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-family: inherit; }

	.results { padding-top: 1em; }
	.results h2 { margin-bottom: 0.5em; }
	.results h3 { margin-top: 1.75em; margin-bottom: 0.4em; }
	.total-score { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.5em; margin: 1em 0; }
	#total-score-value { font-size: 3.5em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); line-height: 1; }
	.total-score-label { color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-size: 1.1em; }
	.score-interp { font-size: 1em; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 1em; padding: 1em 1.25em; background: var(--accent-light); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 4px; }
	.compare { font-size: 0.92em; color: rgb(var(--gray-dark)); border: 1px dashed rgb(var(--gray-light)); border-radius: 6px; padding: 0.7em 1em; }

	.chart { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5em; margin: 1em 0; }
	.chart :global(.chart-row) { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 12em 1fr 2em; align-items: center; gap: 0.75em; font-size: 0.88em; }
	.chart :global(.chart-label) { text-align: right; color: rgb(var(--gray-dark)); line-height: 1.25; }
	.chart :global(.chart-track) { background: rgb(var(--gray-light)); border-radius: 4px; height: 1.5em; overflow: hidden; }
	.chart :global(.chart-bar) { height: 100%; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 4px; min-width: 2px; transition: width 0.4s ease; }
	.chart :global(.chart-val) { font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); text-align: right; }

	.results-disclaimer { font-size: 0.88em; color: rgb(var(--gray-dark)); border-top: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); padding-top: 1.5em; margin-top: 2em; line-height: 1.6; }
	.results-disclaimer h3 { font-size: 1em; color: rgb(var(--black)); margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.5em; }
	.results-disclaimer a { color: var(--accent); }
	.back-btn { background: none; border: 1px solid rgb(var(--gray-light)); padding: 0.6em 1.25em; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 0.95em; cursor: pointer; color: rgb(var(--gray)); font-family: inherit; margin-top: 1.5em; }
	.back-btn:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }

	@media (max-width: 600px) {
		.symptom, .context { padding: 0.8em 0.9em; }
		.segmented { gap: 0.2em; max-width: none; }
		.segmented label { font-size: 0.75em; }
		.chart :global(.chart-row) { grid-template-columns: 8em 1fr 1.6em; gap: 0.5em; font-size: 0.8em; }
	}
</style>
